      "events": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "delta": "**What I changed**\n\nOne thing only: I called `set_status` with `Ready` to move the **Demo orchard** release from Paused to Ready. No deploy action was taken, and nothing else on the panel was modified.\n\n**What the screenshot establishes**\n\nThe captured panel reads:\n\n- `Project: Demo orchard` \u2014 correct target.\n- `Status: Ready` \u2014 the status change took effect; it is no longer Paused.\n- `[ Deploy ]` and `[ Cancel ]` \u2014 both controls remain visible, so enabling Ready did not hide the action buttons.\n- `Last check: All 12 checks passed` \u2014 the panel's most recent recorded check result is a full 12/12 pass.\n\n**Caveats worth flagging**\n\n- The 12/12 line is labeled \"Last check,\" which is a record of the previous check run, not necessarily a check re-executed by my status change. The screenshot confirms that result is *displayed*, not that my action re-ran or re-validated the checks. If you need confirmation that the checks passed *against the current Ready state*, a fresh check run would be required.\n- A screenshot establishes what the UI renders at capture time; it does not independently verify the underlying release state beyond what the panel reports.\n- The panel says nothing about deployment \u2014 the presence of a Deploy button is not a deployment, and I did not press it.\n\n**Net result:** status is Ready, Deploy and Cancel are still available, and the panel shows 12/12 checks passed. Everything is staged for deployment, but nothing has been deployed."
        },
        {
          "type": "done",
          "stop-reason": "end-turn"
        }
      ],
